Scripts to install epics and support modules for LIBI, except areaDetector.

It is recommended to use docker instead.

This repo is still necessary because assemble synapps and vcom driver for docker images are downloaded from here

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------




prepare your machine for ssh communication so you can use xTerm:
	sudo apt-get install ssh

prepare your machine for git and github:
	sudo apt-get install git-all -y
	git config --global user.email "e-mail"
    git config --global user.name "name"
	ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "e-mail"  (server mail is liis.zef.irb@gmail.com, but use yours for your Linux machine)
	> Enter file in which to save the key (/c/Users/YOU/.ssh/id_ALGORITHM):[Press enter for default]
	> Enter passphrase (empty for no passphrase): [Press enter]
	> Enter same passphrase again: [Press enter]
	cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
Copy the complete cat output and login to github and click your icon in the top right -> settings -> SSH and GPG keys -> New SSH key:
Title: <anything>
Key type: Authentication Key
Key: <paste>
Add SSH key

git clone git@github.com:liis-zef-irb/installationScripts.git
cd installationScripts
chmod +x install_epics.sh
./install_epics.sh

relax... it might take half an hour..
check file synApps_libi.txt if everything you need is included. If you include something more you might need some new packages from apt-get

source ~/.bashrc
chmod +x install_synApps.sh
./install_synApps.sh

Adding modules and updating synApps:

- Edit synApps_libi.txt to add what you need
- chmod +x update_synApps.sh
- ./update_synApps.sh

Optional:

- Install VCOM driver:
chmod +x install_VcomDriver.sh
/bin/bash ./install_VcomDriver.sh
- Allow your user to use serial communication; needs user relog
sudo usermod -aG dialout epics   # or whatever is your username

- Clone LIBI IOCs:
cd ${EPICS_ROOT}
git clone git@github.com:liis-zef-irb/IOCs.git


